{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks, Elena. I've reviewed the draft from a privacy perspective, and I have several required changes. First, the vendor's right to use submitted content to improve its services is a problem — our approved data-processing standard prohibits use of customer content for model training or service improvement, so that clause needs to be struck. Second, the 30-day deletion window is insufficient; our standard requires deletion within exactly 7 calendar days after termination. Third, the lack of a specified data-residency location needs to be addressed — our standard requires processing exclusively in the European Union, so we need an explicit data-residency commitment to that effect. These are all mandatory under our approved data-processing standard given that the platform will be processing identifiable customer call transcripts. Let me share the specifics of my findings so everyone has the full picture."}
```

